**`apply_patch` silently replaces all file-configured endpoints when env/CLI provides a URL**

When `WebhookConfigPatch` carries a `Some(endpoint)` (from `CUBE_API_WEBHOOK_URL` or `--webhook-url`), `apply_patch` unconditionally replaces `self.endpoints` with `vec![endpoint]`. A user who configures multiple endpoints in the TOML file and then sets `CUBE_API_WEBHOOK_URL` as a convenience will silently lose all file endpoints.

The auto-enable logic on line 279 compounds this: setting a URL without `enabled` implicitly enables the webhook, so the user gets a *different single-endpoint config* instead of their multi-endpoint setup.

**Suggestion:** Log a warning when endpoint replacement occurs:
```rust
if let Some(endpoint) = patch.endpoint {
    if !self.endpoints.is_empty() {
        warn!("replacing {} file endpoint(s) with 1 env/CLI endpoint", self.endpoints.len());
    }
    self.endpoints = vec![endpoint];
}
```

