review_comments.body:
**SSRF risk — webhook endpoint URL is not validated beyond "must not be empty"**

The endpoint URL is accepted as-is and passed directly to `client.post(&endpoint.url)` in `http.rs:264`. There's no validation for:

- Scheme (should be restricted to `http`/`https`)
- Private/reserved IP ranges (e.g., `169.254.169.254`, `127.0.0.1`, `10.x.x.x`)
- Host or domain format

This creates a Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vector: an attacker who controls the webhook config can make CubeAPI POST structured event data to internal cloud metadata endpoints, internal Kubernetes services, or loopback to CubeAPI itself.

**Suggestion:** Add URL validation in `validate()`:
```rust
pub fn validate(&self) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    for endpoint in &self.endpoints {
        let parsed = url::Url::parse(&endpoint.url)
            .context("invalid webhook URL")?;
        if parsed.scheme() != "http" && parsed.scheme() != "https" {
            bail!("webhook URL scheme must be http or https");
        }
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

Also set `.redirect(reqwest::redirect::Policy::none())` on the `reqwest::Client` builder in `http.rs` to prevent redirect-based SSRF amplification.

