review_comments.body:
**`data.to_vec()` clones on every binary frame from the browser**

`data` is an owned `Vec<u8>` from `Message::Binary(data)`. Calling `data.to_vec()` clones the entire buffer and drops the original on the next line. Every keystroke or program output triggers an allocation + full memcpy that is trivially avoidable.

```rust
// Current — allocation + copy on every frame
if stdin_tx.try_send(data.to_vec()).is_err() {

// Fix — move the owned data directly
if stdin_tx.try_send(data).is_err() {
```

`try_send` takes ownership and returns the value inside the error on failure, but since the input is dropped on overflow anyway, there's no downside.

