review_comments.body:
**Critical: Missing initial connect request — terminal shell will never start**

The `body_stream` sent to envd at lines 430-434 contains only stdin frames and an end-of-stream marker. The initial `ProcessStartRequest` that tells envd to start `/bin/bash -l` is never included in the stream.

The function `proxy::build_connect_request("/bin/bash", &["-l"])` at `proxy.rs:203` exists and is well-tested, but it is **dead code** — nothing calls it outside the test module.

Without this frame, envd will receive raw keystrokes as the first message on the Connect stream and will have no idea what command to run.

**Fix:** Prepend the connect request frame to the stream:
```rust
let connect_req = proxy::build_connect_request("/bin/bash", &["-l".to_string()]);
let connect_req_bytes = serde_json::to_vec(&connect_req)?;
let body_stream = futures::stream::once(async {
    Ok::<_, std::io::Error>(proxy::encode_frame(proxy::FLAG_DATA, &connect_req_bytes))
}).chain(
    tokio_stream::wrappers::ReceiverStream::new(stdin_rx)
        .map(|chunk| Ok::<_, std::io::Error>(proxy::encode_stdin_frame(&chunk)))
).chain(futures::stream::once(async {
    Ok::<_, std::io::Error>(proxy::encode_end_stream_frame())
}));
```

