review_comments.body:
**Critical: `select/default` silently drops events when channel is full**

This non-blocking send on the events channel drops filesystem events if the consumer is reading slower than event production. For `WatchDir` — a change-notification API with no replay mechanism — this is **silent data loss**. The same pattern on lines 589-592, 598-601, and 608-611 also drops errors the same way.

Recommended fix — change to blocking send with context cancellation so backpressure propagates to the server:
```go
if frame.Filesystem != nil {
    select {
    case w.events <- *frame.Filesystem:
    case <-w.ctx.Done():
        return
    }
}
```

