review_comments.body:
**The inner loop over `GetVolumeSources()` silently passes if all sources have empty HostPath.**

At line 367, the `for` loop iterates every `HostDirSource` but returns the same per-volume error regardless of which source triggers it. Worse, if all sources have an empty `HostPath` (or the slice is empty), the loop body never executes and the function falls through — meaning a **writable** host_dir volume with no valid source entries would **incorrectly pass validation**.

Since the error is already scoped to the volume (line 369), the per-source iteration adds complexity without value and introduces a latent false-negative:

```go
// Before (current — silent pass on empty/malformed sources):
for _, hostDir := range hostDirs.GetVolumeSources() {
    if hostDir != nil && hostDir.GetHostPath() != "" {
        return fmt.Errorf("writable host_dir volume %s is not supported by CommitSandbox", volume.GetName())
    }
}

// After (direct volume-level check, no silent pass):
if _, writable := writableVolumes[volume.GetName()]; writable {
    return fmt.Errorf("writable host_dir volume %s is not supported by CommitSandbox", volume.GetName())
}
```

If per-source granularity is planned for future error messages, at minimum add a comment explaining why the iteration exists — without it, the loop reads as dead complexity.

